From: SamuriHL <samurihl@msn.com>
Subject: [PATCH] BD-J: report the 2160p video size

StreamInfo.getVideoSize() has no break after the 2160p case (video
format 0x08), so it falls through to "default: return null" for every
UHD stream. VideoControl.getInputVideoSize() passes the null on, and
setClipRegion() dereferences it (VideoControl.java:119). BD-J Xlets
that size or clip the background video then throw: on M3GAN 2.0 UHD,
Top Menu during the feature raised NullPointerException from
BackgroundVideoPresentationControlImpl.setSize() in the Xlet's tearDown,
setVideoResolution, setGraphicsResolution and setBackgroundResolution
handlers.

Add the missing break. getInputVideoSize() also treats a format that
StreamInfo does not know as "no size", as it already does for a missing
stream, so callers get their existing 0x0 path instead of a null.

Unchanged in libbluray 1.5.1 and master.

diff -ruN a/src/libbluray/bdj/java/org/videolan/StreamInfo.java b/src/libbluray/bdj/java/org/videolan/StreamInfo.java
--- a/src/libbluray/bdj/java/org/videolan/StreamInfo.java	2026-09-25 16:49:46.421563732 -0400
+++ b/src/libbluray/bdj/java/org/videolan/StreamInfo.java	2026-09-25 16:49:46.475927982 -0400
@@ -73,6 +73,7 @@
         case (byte)0x08:
             width = 3840;
             height = 2160;
+            break;
         default:
                 return null;
         }
diff -ruN a/src/libbluray/bdj/java/org/videolan/media/content/playlist/VideoControl.java b/src/libbluray/bdj/java/org/videolan/media/content/playlist/VideoControl.java
--- a/src/libbluray/bdj/java/org/videolan/media/content/playlist/VideoControl.java	2026-09-25 16:49:46.421908370 -0400
+++ b/src/libbluray/bdj/java/org/videolan/media/content/playlist/VideoControl.java	2026-09-25 16:49:46.476164159 -0400
@@ -82,7 +82,10 @@
         StreamInfo stream = getCurrentStream();
         if (stream == null)
             return new Dimension(0, 0);
-        return stream.getVideoSize();
+        Dimension size = stream.getVideoSize();
+        if (size == null)
+            return new Dimension(0, 0);
+        return size;
     }
 
     public Dimension getVideoSize() {
